{"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event type names the purpose it is collected for, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"consentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless its ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event(consent:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says otherwise. Give the tracker a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Consent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the app updates as the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decides, and an event reaches a destination only once its category is granted:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Event(consent: .advertising)","struct AdClicked {","    var campaign: String","}","","let consent = Consent([.analytics: .granted])","let tracker = Tracker(consent: consent)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: ConsoleDestination(),","    ConsoleDestination().accepting(.advertising)",")","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))          \/\/ delivered: analytics is granted","tracker.track(AdClicked(campaign: \"spring\"))  \/\/ held: advertising is undecided","consent.grant(.advertising)                   \/\/ delivers the held AdClicked"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker given no consent delivers every event."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Undecided, granted and denied","anchor":"Undecided-granted-and-denied"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A category is undecided until the app grants or denies it. While it is undecided, its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held in memory, not written to a store, up to "},{"code":"heldRecordLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" records (1,000 by default) across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every category, the oldest dropped first when the hold is full. Granting delivers them in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were tracked, before anything tracked after the grant. Denying drops them. Events tracked while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their category is denied are never collected."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grant"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deny"},{"type":"text","text":" return at once: they record the decision, and the tracker’s worker releases or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops what it held. Every drop of a record that was held or kept is reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent.dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" as it happens, so none is lost silently. Held"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records are lost if the app ends first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Records that a store recovered from an earlier run are gated again as the tracker starts. They are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held outside the bound, since the store still keeps them, and the store forgets each one that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Destinations","anchor":"Destinations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A destination receives every category the consent lets through, unless ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"text":" narrows it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the categories it serves, as the second destination above takes only advertising.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Consent Gating","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"role":"article","title":"Persisting Records","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WritingAVendorDestination":{"role":"article","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","abstract":[{"text":"Send events to an analytics vendor Traffluent doesn’t cover yet, from a module of your own, with the same rules as the destinations it ships.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Defining Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"abstract":[{"text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Sampling Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"}}}